{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2064","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Remove the Ends"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-zero"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. Initially, you have $$$0$$$ coins, and you will do the following until $$$a$$$ is empty: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let $$$m$$$ be the current size of $$$a$$$. Select an integer $$$i$$$ where $$$1 \\le i \\le m$$$, gain $$$|a_i|$$$$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ coins, and then: "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"kind":"list"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$a_i \\lt 0$$$, then replace $$$a$$$ with $$$[a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_{i - 1}]$$$ (that is, delete the suffix beginning with $$$a_i$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise, replace $$$a$$$ with $$$[a_{i + 1},a_{i + 2},\\ldots,a_m]$$$ (that is, delete the prefix ending with $$$a_i$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the maximum number of coins you can have at the end of the process."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$Here $$$|a_i|$$$ represents the absolute value of $$$a_i$$$: it equals $$$a_i$$$ when $$$a_i \\gt 0$$$ and $$$-a_i$$$ when $$$a_i \\lt 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each testcase contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$, $$$a_i \\ne 0$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sum of $$$n$$$ across all testcases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output the maximum number of coins you can have at the end of the process."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n6\n3 1 4 -1 -5 -9\n6\n-10 -3 -17 1 19 20\n1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n23\n40\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An example of how to get $$$23$$$ coins in the first testcase is as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [3, 1, 4, -1, -5, \\color{red}{-9}] \\xrightarrow{i = 6} a = [3, 1, 4, -1, -5] $$$, and get $$$9$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [\\color{red}{3}, 1, 4, -1, -5] \\xrightarrow{i = 1} a = [1, 4, -1, -5] $$$, and get $$$3$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [\\color{red}{1}, 4, -1, -5] \\xrightarrow{i = 1} a = [4, -1, -5] $$$, and get $$$1$$$ coin. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [4, -1, \\color{red}{-5}] \\xrightarrow{i = 3} a = [4, -1] $$$, and get $$$5$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [4, \\color{red}{-1}] \\xrightarrow{i = 2} a = [4] $$$, and get $$$1$$$ coin. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [\\color{red}{4}] \\xrightarrow{i = 1} a = [] $$$, and get $$$4$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" After all the operations, you have $$$23$$$ coins."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An example of how to get $$$40$$$ coins in the second testcase is as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [-10, -3, -17, \\color{red}{1}, 19, 20] \\xrightarrow{i = 4} a = [19, 20] $$$, and get $$$1$$$ coin. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [\\color{red}{19}, 20] \\xrightarrow{i = 1} a = [20] $$$, and get $$$19$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a = [\\color{red}{20}] \\xrightarrow{i = 1} a = [] $$$, and get $$$20$$$ coins. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" After all the operations, you have $$$40$$$ coins."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2064C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2064/problem/C"}